Wayfinder Agent — Job 4
Present Waystar Support (Current State)
Today, support for missing remits, user access, and security-related issues is handled manually by administrative or IT support teams. Tasks include:

Assisting clients with missing remittance files or payment posting questions.

Helping users reset passwords or recover locked accounts.

Managing permission sets and role assignments, including enabling or revoking access.

Supporting two-factor authentication (2FA) setup and recovery.

Managing account-level access, IP restrictions, and compliance settings.

Reviewing audit logs and login history to investigate security events.

These tasks often require back-and-forth verification steps, manual email responses, and involve significant operational overhead, leading to longer resolution times and potential compliance risks.

Agent Execution (Proposed State)
🌟 What the agent will do
Automate guidance and resolution for missing remittance inquiries, including checking status, confirming availability, or initiating a resend.

Assist users with password resets, following secure verification workflows, and explain password policy requirements.

Guide users through permission and role understanding — help them identify current permissions, request changes, or understand access rights.

Support secure 2FA setup and recovery steps, reducing manual IT intervention.

Provide detailed login and audit history upon request (e.g., "When did I last log in?").

Address basic account-level security configurations, such as IP restrictions and access policies.

Escalate high-risk or unresolved security issues (e.g., suspected unauthorized access, Domain Admin lockouts) directly to IT/security teams.

💬 Agent Tasks and Data Sources
Data Sources:

User Management module (Users screen, Permissions tab, Roles tab, Reset Password, 2FA tab, Login history).

Security module (Permission Sets, IP restrictions, password and account policies).

Remits module (Remittance files, Payment posting screens).

Agent Tasks:

Retrieve and verify user account details securely before initiating actions.

Show assigned roles and permissions, help explain or adjust access as per policy.

Initiate password reset and guide through policy-compliant password creation.

Help configure or recover two-factor authentication, provide security best practices.

Address missing remit requests by checking remittance file statuses and triggering resends if allowed.

Provide or clarify login history and security audit logs.

Manage escalations seamlessly to IT/security teams when required.

